Yes. This repo already has build scripts/workflows for both.

Android
Recommended: build Android from WSL/Linux or Git Bash, not plain PowerShell, because the repo scripts are .sh.

Prerequisites
Install:

Android Studio
Android SDK + NDK
CMake
Ninja or Make
Git Bash/WSL tools: bash, wget, unzip, tar
Find your NDK path, usually like:

C:\Users\aaa\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\ndk\<version>
In Git Bash/WSL, set it:

export ANDROID_NDK=/c/Users/aaa/AppData/Local/Android/Sdk/ndk/<version>
From repo root:

cd /e/dataToExport/vtran/fromshc/sherpa-onnx-master
Build Android libraries
For common Android ABIs:

export ANDROID_NDK=/c/Users/aaa/AppData/Local/Android/Sdk/ndk/<version>
export SHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_C_API=ON
./build-android-arm64-v8a.sh
./build-android-armv7-eabi.sh
./build-android-x86-64.sh
./build-android-x86.sh
Outputs are under:

build-android-arm64-v8a/install/lib
build-android-armv7-eabi/install/lib
build-android-x86-64/install/lib
build-android-x86/install/lib
For Android Studio JNI usage, copy the .so files into:

app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/
app/src/main/jniLibs/armeabi-v7a/
app/src/main/jniLibs/x86_64/
app/src/main/jniLibs/x86/
Important: with the default shared build, copy both:

libsherpa-onnx-jni.so
libonnxruntime.so
If you want a single JNI library with ONNX Runtime linked statically:

export BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF
./build-android-arm64-v8a.sh
Then you mostly need:

libsherpa-onnx-jni.so
Build Android AAR
The CI builds an AAR from:

android/SherpaOnnxAar
After building/copying jniLibs, run:

cd android/SherpaOnnxAar
./gradlew :sherpa_onnx:assembleRelease
Output:

android/SherpaOnnxAar/sherpa_onnx/build/outputs/aar/sherpa_onnx-release.aar
Windows
Use Developer PowerShell for Visual Studio 2022 or x64 Native Tools Command Prompt.

Prerequisites
Install:

Visual Studio 2022 with “Desktop development with C++”
CMake
Git
From repo root:

cd e:\dataToExport\vtran\fromshc\sherpa-onnx-master
mkdir build
cd build
Windows x64 Release build
cmake -A x64 `
  -DSHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_TTS=ON `
  -DSHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_PORTAUDIO=OFF `
  -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON `
  -DSHERPA_ONNX_USE_STATIC_CRT=OFF `
  -DBUILD_ESPEAK_NG_EXE=OFF `
  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=./install `
  ..
cmake --build . --config Release -- /m:2
cmake --build . --config Release --target install -- /m:2
Output:

build\install\bin
build\install\lib
build\install\include
Main executable:

build\install\bin\sherpa-onnx.exe
Windows ARM64 or x86
Only change the -A value:

-A ARM64
or:

-A Win32
Static library build
For static libs:

-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF
For static MSVC runtime:


-DSHERPA_ONNX_USE_STATIC_CRT=ON
My Suggested Starting Point
For Android, start with only:

export SHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_C_API=ON
./build-android-arm64-v8a.sh
For Windows, start with:

-A x64
-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON
-DSHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_TTS=ON
That gives you the most common Android ABI and a normal Windows x64 package first.

